It is Sunday afternoon.
I am sitting on a bench in the park.
I am eating a warm bun maska.
Asha's dog Moti is sitting near me.
He is looking at me.
His eyes are big and sad.
He also wants the bun maska.
I say, "No, Moti, stay here."
"You must not eat this."
"Dogs must not eat human food."
"This is Asha's rule."
I take out a special food item for him from my bag.
I say, "Moti, come here."
"Look at this, take it."
He comes close.
He eats it quickly.
Now Moti is happy.
He does not look at my food again.
I also eat my bun maska in peace.
